From a8c47a41e2df74cf37474f3ba9044e804cb9d380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luke <luke@devmindscape.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:33:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Add optional overlay scroll bars on PGTK

GTK applications use overlay scroll bars: thin indicators drawn over
the content that appear while scrolling or when the pointer is near,
and fade out.  GTK only provides them inside GtkScrolledWindow, which
Emacs doesn't use, so implement the behavior for Emacs' own scroll
bars, using the theme's style for them.

* src/pgtkterm.c (OVERLAY_SCROLL_BAR_DELAY)
(OVERLAY_SCROLL_BAR_FADE_INTERVAL, OVERLAY_SCROLL_BAR_FADE_STEPS)
(OVERLAY_SCROLL_BAR_PROXIMITY): New macros.
(struct overlay_scroll_bar): New structure.
(overlay_scroll_bar_state, overlay_scroll_bar_free)
(overlay_scroll_bar_fade, overlay_scroll_bar_start_fade)
(overlay_scroll_bar_reveal, overlay_scroll_bar_crossing)
(overlay_scroll_bar_button, pgtk_overlay_scroll_bar_pointer)
(watch_pgtk_overlay_scroll_bars): New functions.
(pgtk_setup_overlay_scroll_bar): New function.
(pgtk_set_vertical_scroll_bar): Place overlay scroll bars over the
edge of the window's text, don't clear under them, and show them when
the window scrolls.
(motion_notify_event): Show overlay scroll bars near the pointer.
(pgtk_new_font): Don't reserve columns for overlay scroll bars.
(syms_of_pgtkterm) <pgtk-overlay-scroll-bars>: New variable.
* src/pgtkterm.h (pgtk_setup_overlay_scroll_bar): Declare.
* src/pgtkfns.c (pgtk_set_scroll_bar_default_width): Overlay scroll
bars take no room.
* src/gtkutil.c (xg_finish_scroll_bar_creation): Set up overlay scroll
bars.
(xg_get_scroll_bar_widget): New function.
(xg_update_scrollbar_pos): Don't show, clear under, lower or garbage
the frame for overlay scroll bars.
* src/gtkutil.h (xg_get_scroll_bar_widget): Declare.
* etc/NEWS: Announce 'pgtk-overlay-scroll-bars'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
